Subject: [PATCH] staging: t2bce: run the stateful handshake for hibernation images

The BCE core PM table only exposes suspend and resume. During hibernation the
USB core therefore freezes and restores the VHCI child without invoking the
parent BCE SAVE_STATE_AND_SLEEP and RESTORE_STATE_AND_WAKE handshake. After a
test_resume memory rewind, Linux restores queue indices that no longer match
bridgeOS. Every VHCI queue command times out and usb_dev_restore loses the
internal keyboard and trackpad.

Pair freeze with the existing stateful suspend path and both thaw and restore
with its matching resume path. This makes the in-place test_resume lifecycle
coherent without changing ordinary S3 behavior. It does not implement the
separate no-state reconstruction required after a cold S4 boot.

--- a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
@@ -709,6 +709,9 @@ struct dev_pm_ops t2bce_pci_driver_pm = {
         .prepare = t2bce_prepare,
         .suspend = t2bce_suspend,
         .resume = t2bce_resume,
+        .freeze = t2bce_suspend,
+        .thaw = t2bce_resume,
+        .restore = t2bce_resume,
         .complete = t2bce_complete
 };
 struct pci_driver t2bce_pci_driver = {
